# The example C++ is written in LLVM's style, to match the real code the lessons
# reference (Clang, MLIR, ParserByHand, gazc). The column limit is narrowed to 55.
# Comment reflow is disabled so the deliberately-formatted teaching comments (with
# aligned notes and code sketches) keep their layout; only code is wrapped to 55.
# Constructs that still read worse when trimmed are guarded in-source with
# `// clang-format off` / `// clang-format on`.
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
ColumnLimit: 55
ReflowComments: false
Standard: c++17
